# Line endings are bytes, and in this repository bytes are what the fixtures and the goldens are made of.
#
# With no file like this one, git asks each platform's `core.autocrlf` — and the Git for Windows installer
# defaults that to `true`, so a Windows clone of a commit is a *different tree* than a Linux clone of the
# same commit: every LF in the checkout arrives as CRLF. That is why two dependency-delta tests were red on
# the Windows runner and green on the other two (`reco-d3p9`): one compares a rendered table against a
# reviewed `expected.txt`, and the golden arrived with a `\r` on every line; the other looks for a lockfile
# whose bytes end `}\n` so it can truncate it, and found none, so it asserted a corruption it had never
# made. The product was never wrong — `deps/text.rs`, `deps/hunk.rs` and `deps/yaml.rs` all tolerate CRLF,
# which is the promise under review here.
#
# The policy: text is stored LF and checked out LF on every platform; a file whose exact bytes are the point
# is declared `-text`, which converts in neither direction (an attribute that *normalises* such a file would
# make a clean clone look dirty, because its stored blob is already what the checkout must contain).
#
# --- text is LF everywhere -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- bytes that are the point: no conversion, in either direction --------------------------------------
*.gz      -text
*.zst     -text
*.tar     -text
*.zip     -text
*.pack    -text
*.png     -text
*.jpg     -text
*.jpeg    -text
*.gif     -text
*.ico     -text
*.pdf     -text
*.woff    -text
*.woff2   -text
*.sqlite  -text
*.sqlite3 -text
*.db      -text
*.bin     -text
*.dll     -text
*.exe     -text
*.lib     -text
*.a       -text
*.so      -text
*.dylib   -text

# Fuzz seeds are inputs, not documents: a seed whose newlines were rewritten is a different input, and the
# corpus is supposed to mean the same coverage on Windows that it means here.
fuzz/corpus/** -text

# --- the committed CR that is load-bearing -------------------------------------------------------------
# The CRLF-churn fixture the diff viewer's "every line changed, and the marker says why" golden is drawn
# from: the carriage returns are the fixture (and deliberately mixed with lines that have none), so the
# bytes are pinned rather than restyled. See `crates/fathom-tui/tests/diff_golden.rs`.
crates/fathom-tui/tests/fixtures/crlf.diff -text
crates/fathom-tui/tests/fixtures/empty.diff -text

# cargo-dist's WiX source, committed as its generator wrote it (CRLF). `dist plan` refuses to run against a
# generated file that is not its generator's byte-for-byte output — a whitespace touch once stopped the
# whole release pipeline — so these bytes are left exactly as stored.
crates/fathom-cli/wix/main.wxs -text
